<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Osorkon the Elder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> · Also known as Osochor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Osorkon the Elder was a king of the Twenty-first Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the late 10th century BCE, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanis">Tanis</a> for about six years. He was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of Libyan descent, a member of the Meshwesh chiefly family settled at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bubastis">Bubastis</a> and an uncle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shoshenq-i">Shoshenq I</a>. His reign foreshadowed the Libyan dynasties that ruled Egypt for the next two centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/osorkon-the-elder.jpg" alt="Osorkon the Elder" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khruner · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Block_Aakheperre_Osorkon_by_Khruner.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
